==English==
[[Image:Julia balcony.jpg|thumb|right|A balcony.]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbælkəni/}}
* {{audio|en-us-balcony.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|balcone|lang=it}} "balcony, floor-length window" from Old {{etyl|it|-}} {{term|balcone|lang=it}} "scaffold", from {{etyl|lng|en}} *{{term||balko, *balkon-|beam|lang=lng|sc=Latn}}  from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|balkô||beam|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bhelg'-||beam, pile, prop|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|balco|balco, balcho|lang=goh|beam}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|balca||beam, ridge|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|balk}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=balconies}}

# An accessible [[structure]] extending from a [[building]], especially outside a window.
# {{rfquotek|Shakespeare}}
# {{rfquotek|the Bible}}
# An accessible structure [[overlook]]ing a stage.

